      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In supporting the expansion of executive privilege as a necessary protection for the presidency, you can argue that the doctrine of executive privilege is a constitutional inherent power granted by Article II, Section 1 of the US Constitution, as well as a cornerstone of the separation of powers between the executive and legislative branches. This privilege allows the President to maintain confidentiality of high-level discussions and prevent congressional overreach, safeguarding national security and intra-branch confidentiality. By invoking executive privilege, the President can protect sensitive information from compelled disclosure, thereby preserving the integrity of their decision-making process.",
